---
import { Font } from "astro:assets";
import "../styles/global.css";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  plain?: boolean;
}

const { title, description, plain = false } = Astro.props;
const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
// A preview must never be indexed or compete with the real domain.
const preview = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PREVIEW === "1";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="ru">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    {preview ? <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" /> : <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />}
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0d1b2a" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="ru_RU" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <link rel="icon" href={withBase("/favicon.svg")} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-display" preload={[{ weight: "300", style: "normal", subset: "cyrillic" }]} />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-body" preload={[{ weight: "400", style: "normal", subset: "cyrillic" }]} />
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var root = document.documentElement;
        if (window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) return;
        root.classList.add("motion");
        // If the motion script never arrives, show everything anyway.
        window.setTimeout(function () {
          if (!window.__motionReady) root.classList.remove("motion");
        }, 3000);
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class:list={{ "is-plain": plain }}>
    {import.meta.env.DEV && <Fragment set:html={`<!--
THESIS: Made to your centimetres. The boutique-lingerie standard played straight, full-bleed photography, a refined serif, a pinned navy-and-greige palette, refusing only the default's stillness: the page moves like a film and measures as it goes.
OWN-WORLD: Palette pinned by the owners: #0D1B2A navy ink and dark fields, #E0E1DD paper, #415A77 slate accent on light, #C7BEB6 greige accent on navy and warm field of the making section. Cormorant 300 display with slate (on light) or greige (on navy) italic emphasis; Montserrat text, tracked uppercase for nav and buttons. Square navy buttons with a rising slate fill. Hairline rules. A centimetre tape with ticks is the one signature device.
STORY: See the lace, understand it is sewn to your own measurements by one maker in Yekaterinburg, see the four steps and the work, see how many slots remain, write through VK, MAX, phone or Avito (Telegram last).
FIRST VIEWPORT: Full-bleed lace photograph settling from a clipped frame on navy; wordmark САНТИМА centred on top; headline «Бельё по вашим меркам» bottom-left with «вашим» in greige italic; one lede; primary button «Заказать пошив» leading to the contact channels, secondary link to the process.
FORM: canon, the category standard (standing exit), with elevated cinematic motion; seed key 5308e204.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->`} />}
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Перейти к содержанию</a>
    <Header plain={plain} />
    <main id="main">
      <slot />
    </main>
    <Footer />
    <script>
      import "../scripts/motion.ts";
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
